      "explanation": "**Choice B is correct.** The text says that watching passersby was one of the plaza visitors' favorite activities and quotes Whyte's conclusion: \"What attracts people most, it would appear, is other people.\" Spots where other people already were let visitors do exactly that.\n\n**The Full Solution:**\n- How to spot it: this is a detail question, so the answer must restate something the text says outright.\n- The text links where people sat to what they liked to do: they sat where other people were, and watching passersby was a favorite activity.\n- Whyte's conclusion sums it up: people are drawn to other people. Choice B restates that without adding anything.\n\n**Why the other choices are wrong:**\n- A: The text never compares the seating in different parts of the plazas.\n- C: Shade is never mentioned in the text.\n- D: Food vendors are never mentioned in the text."
